# 4. THE INTERACTIVE MOVIE MAP

THIS IS THE CORE PRODUCT FEATURE.

Build a highly interactive graph visualization.

Every movie is represented as a node.

Relationships are represented as edges connecting nodes.

## Node categories

Create distinct visual representations for:

- Movies.
- Directors.
- Actors.
- Genres.
- Franchises.
- Trilogies.
- Cinematic universes.
- Studios.
- Writers.
- Composers.

Movies should be the primary node type.

Other node types should be available through exploration and filtering.

## Movie node appearance

Each movie node should display:

- Poster thumbnail.
- Movie title.
- Release year.
- Optional rating indicator.

Node size can reflect popularity or user-selected importance.

Allow different visualization modes:

### Poster Mode

Display movie posters as nodes.

This should be the most visually appealing mode.

### Minimal Mode

Display simple colored circles with titles.

Useful for large graphs.

### Genre Mode

Color nodes according to genre.

### Franchise Mode

Group connected movies into recognizable clusters.

### Timeline Mode

Arrange nodes chronologically.

### Relationship Mode

Highlight the connections between selected movies.

## Graph interactions

Users must be able to:

- Pan.
- Zoom.
- Drag nodes.
- Select nodes.
- Expand connections.
- Collapse branches.
- Search within the map.
- Filter relationships.
- Highlight paths.
- Center the graph.
- Reset the visualization.
- Save interesting maps.

Clicking a movie should reveal its details.

Double-clicking or using an expand control should reveal additional connections.

Use smooth transitions.

Avoid overwhelming users with hundreds of nodes simultaneously.

Implement progressive graph expansion.

