# 6. RELATIONSHIP STRENGTH

Not all relationships are equally meaningful.

Create a relationship-weighting system.

For example:

| Relationship | Example Strength |
|---|---:|
| Direct sequel | 100 |
| Same franchise | 95 |
| Same director | 85 |
| Same lead actor | 80 |
| Same trilogy | 100 |
| Same screenwriter | 70 |
| Same genre | 50 |
| Shared themes | 40 |
| Similar visual style | 35 |

These values should be configurable.

The system should distinguish factual relationships from inferred similarities.

For example:

A sequel is a factual relationship.

A similar visual style is an editorial or algorithmic relationship.

Display relationship explanations when users hover over connections.

Example:

"Connected because both movies were directed by Christopher Nolan."

Or:

"Connected through the Cornetto Trilogy."

Avoid presenting subjective recommendations as verified facts.

